  "rationale": "The retained agenda and Granicus player both title this recording as a joint meeting of the Board of Trustees of Eagle Mountain-Saginaw ISD and the Fort Worth City Council (retained-agenda; provider-player), and the chapter index confirms substantive segments for each participant: ISD items (Reports of the Superintendent, EMS ISD Demographic Report, State of the District) and City items (Reports of the City of Fort Worth, Mayor's Report on Education, Mayor's Announcements) (native-source-chapters). Both proven participants are therefore named. Assignments: (1) fort-worth-tx-emsisd-board-joint-meetings is configured exactly for 'Source-scoped joint proceedings of the EMSISD Board and Fort Worth Council; original whole recordings retained,' matching this whole recording; (2) under the joints rule, every proven participant can share the recording in its configured feed, and the Council's configured feed is fort-worth-tx-city-council; (3) the broader fort-worth-tx (Fort Worth — All Meetings) grouping carries Fort Worth Granicus City Council meeting videos and is considered independently of convening. Distractors rejected: the 'State of the District' report is an ISD item, not a State of the City address, so fort-worth-tx-state-of-city does not apply; the Hollenstein opening ceremony is one agenda item within a business meeting, not a standalone ceremony/dedication, and the joint feed retains whole recordings, so no exclude_event. No standalone EMS ISD Board feed exists, but coverage is supplied by the configured joint feed, so no unconfigured_body disposition is needed. Publication action: assign_existing."
